[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Start "french-rubinstein-nf6 4.Nxe4"]
[Name "4...Nc6: the knight first"]

4... Nc6
5. Nf3 { Guards d4, which the knight has just hit. [%cal Gf3d4] }
5... Nf6
( 5... e5? { Opens the game with the king still in the centre. The knight on c6 can now be pinned. }
  6. Bb5 { Pins the knight, and e5 has lost its guard. [%cal Gb5e8] }
  6... Ne7
  7. O-O { Castles while Black can't. Material is level, but the e5 pawn is loose and Black is well behind in development. The engine has White more than two pawns ahead: the gain is positional. } )
6. Nxf6+ { The same swap, so the queen comes to f6. }
6... Qxf6 { And the position is the one from the queen trap, with White to move: Bd3 is the move. }
7. Bd3 * 
